{
  "_doc": "Rappel Lab (Project Redmond R4.1, DECISIONS D-201): a practice yard with every kind of face a rope hangs on, built for the rappel rules and their tests (game/shared/test/rappel.test.ts). Same format as movement_lab: metres, Y up, yawDeg 0 faces -Z. The Tower (one rope up three storeys, a 2F window with nothing under it, a barricaded door, stepped gables over its top), the Step House (its 2F wall 8 cm further out than its 1F wall), the Ledge House (its 2F set back 0.3 m behind a ledge, two windows over the ledge and over the Annex roof, a balcony behind a railing), the Annex (a one-storey roof under a soft wall) and the Eave House (a roof hanging over its walls). The rappel zones are the faces (level/rappel.ts): a thin box just outside each outside wall, one per storey. Sizes are lab choices, not measurements.",
